<#
.SYNOPSIS
    [Runbook 9] Reports SharePoint sharing exposure - anonymous links,
    organization-wide links, and external/guest access - on every document
    library of every site in the tenant. Microsoft Graph only, no
    PnP.PowerShell dependency anywhere in this script.

.DESCRIPTION
    This is a *sharing exposure* audit, not a full permissions audit -
    complements Runbook 8 (8-Audit-SharePointSitePermissions.ps1), which
    reports Site Collection Administrators and Owners/Members/Visitors group
    membership via PnP. That data is NOT obtainable from Microsoft Graph
    today - there is no Graph endpoint for SharePoint's classic group model
    (no site collection admins, no Owners/Members/Visitors rosters, no
    "has unique role assignments" flag on the site/web). Confirmed current
    limitation, not an oversight in this script. If you need that data, it
    still has to come from Runbook 8.

    What Graph DOES give us, and what this script reports instead: every
    direct permission grant and every sharing link on the ROOT of each
    document library (drive) in each site, via
    GET /sites/{id}/drives/{id}/root/permissions. For each permission found:

      - PermissionType: AnonymousLink / OrganizationLink / OtherLink / Direct
      - Who it's granted to (direct grantee email, redeemed link users, or a
        pending sharing invitation email)
      - IsExternal - grantee's email domain checked against the tenant's
        verified domains (via GET /organization, covered by the
        Directory.Read.All permission already granted to the managed
        identity for the other runbooks - no extra scope needed for this
        part)
      - HasPassword / ExpirationDateTime on links
      - Roles (read/write/owner)

    Scope and known gaps (read before treating "no findings" as "no risk"):
      - Item/list/file-level unique permissions and individual document
        sharing links are NOT enumerated - only the drive ROOT. A per-file
        crawl tenant-wide is a different order of magnitude of Graph calls
        and belongs in its own scoped script if ever needed.
      - Site Collection Administrators and the default permission groups are
        out of scope here - see Runbook 8.
      - A site can have more than one drive (multiple document libraries);
        this script checks all of them, not just "Documents".

.NOTES
    Managed identity needs:
      Sites.Read.All          Graph app permission - NEW, not yet granted.
                               Add to the same CR addendum already tracking
                               RoleManagement.Read.Directory and
                               Reports.Read.All (see prod-cutover notes) -
                               this is the third scope going beyond the
                               signed CR's original 3-permission list.
      Directory.Read.All      already granted (Sept 3) - reused here for the
                               verified-domains lookup, no new grant needed.
      Mail.Send                already granted - report delivery.

    Deliberately uses ONLY Microsoft.Graph.Authentication + raw
    Invoke-MgGraphRequest calls - no Microsoft.Graph.Sites /
    Microsoft.Graph.Files typed cmdlets, and critically no PnP.PowerShell.
    That means this script has NO PowerShell-version floor: it runs fine on
    the current PS 7.2 Automation Account runtime as well as a future 7.4
    Runtime Environment, unlike Runbook 8 / Runbook 2 / the new
    site-permissions script, which are all pinned to PnP.PowerShell 2.12.0
    specifically because PnP 3.x needs PS 7.4.6+ (see the Sept 9 PnP
    incident notes). This script sidesteps that whole problem - it is not
    affected by the pending 7.2-vs-7.4 runtime decision either way.

    Enumeration: GET /sites/getAllSites (requires Sites.Read.All,
    application-only - this is the same endpoint the Get-MgAllSite cmdlet
    wraps). This is NOT the same as /sites?search=* , which misses sites
    with no crawled/indexed content and behaves inconsistently for this kind
    of tenant-wide sweep.

    Performance: one Graph call per site to list drives, one call per drive
    (plus pagination) to list root permissions. Lighter than Runbook 8 (no
    per-site PnP connection overhead) but still scales with site count x
    drive count. Start $MaxSitesToProcess small to time a run before
    trusting a schedule, same as Runbook 8.

    Throttling: Invoke-GraphRequestWithRetry below does exponential backoff
    on 429/503/504 rather than a fixed Start-Sleep between every call - Graph
    read throttling is bursty, a flat delay either wastes time when there is
    no pressure or is not long enough when there is.
#>

# ===================== CONFIG =====================
$IncludeOneDriveSites   = $false                                   # EDIT - personal OneDrive sites are usually out of scope for this audit
$ExcludedUrlPatterns    = @("*/sites/appcatalog*")                  # EDIT - wildcards matched against Site URL
$FlagAnonymousLinks     = $true                                     # anonymous ("anyone") links always flagged for review
$FlagOrganizationLinks  = $true                                     # org-wide ("anyone in company") links flagged for review too
$MaxNamesPerCell        = 25                                         # cap grantee emails listed per CSV cell before "+N more"
$MaxSitesToProcess      = 0                                          # EDIT - 0 = no limit; set a small number (e.g. 25) to time-test a run first
$SenderMailbox          = "m365-audits@yourtenant.com"               # EDIT
$ReportRecipients       = @("secops@yourtenant.com")                 # EDIT
# ==================================================

Import-Module Microsoft.Graph.Authentication
# NOTE: this dot-source only resolves when the file sits next to a Common\
# folder (local testing layout, see README.md). Pasted into an Azure
# Automation runbook there is no filesystem, so either inline the
# Send-ReportEmail function above this line, or publish it as a module and
# Import-Module it instead - same caveat as every other script in this set.
. (Join-Path $PSScriptRoot "Common\Send-ReportEmail.ps1")

function ConvertTo-JoinedNames {
    param([string[]]$Names, [int]$MaxNames)
    if (-not $Names -or $Names.Count -eq 0) { return "" }
    $unique = $Names | Sort-Object -Unique
    if ($unique.Count -le $MaxNames) { return ($unique -join "; ") }
    $shown = $unique | Select-Object -First $MaxNames
    return ("{0}; +{1} more" -f ($shown -join "; "), ($unique.Count - $MaxNames))
}

function Invoke-GraphRequestWithRetry {
    param([string]$Uri, [string]$Method = "GET", [int]$MaxRetries = 5)
    $attempt = 0
    while ($true) {
        try {
            return Invoke-MgGraphRequest -Method $Method -Uri $Uri -ErrorAction Stop
        }
        catch {
            $attempt++
            $msg = $_.Exception.Message
            $isThrottleOrTransient = $msg -match '429|TooManyRequests|503|504|ServiceUnavailable|GatewayTimeout'
            if ($isThrottleOrTransient -and $attempt -le $MaxRetries) {
                $backoffSeconds = [math]::Min(60, [math]::Pow(2, $attempt))
                Write-Warning "Graph request throttled/transient error (attempt $attempt/$MaxRetries) - backing off $backoffSeconds s. Uri: $Uri"
                Start-Sleep -Seconds $backoffSeconds
                continue
            }
            throw
        }
    }
}

function Get-GraphCollection {
    param([string]$Uri)
    $results = New-Object System.Collections.Generic.List[object]
    $nextUri = $Uri
    while ($nextUri) {
        $resp = Invoke-GraphRequestWithRetry -Uri $nextUri
        if ($resp.value) { $results.AddRange([object[]]$resp.value) }
        $nextUri = $resp.'@odata.nextLink'
    }
    return $results
}

Connect-MgGraph -Identity   # uses the Automation Account's managed identity, no prompts

$tempDir   = [System.IO.Path]::GetTempPath()
$timestamp = Get-Date -Format "yyyy-MM-dd_HHmm"
$outFile   = Join-Path $tempDir "SharePointSharingExposure_$timestamp.csv"

# ---- Verified domains, for the external-grantee check ---------------------
$verifiedDomains = @()
try {
    $org = Invoke-GraphRequestWithRetry -Uri "https://graph.microsoft.com/v1.0/organization?`$select=verifiedDomains"
    if ($org.value -and $org.value[0].verifiedDomains) {
        $verifiedDomains = $org.value[0].verifiedDomains | ForEach-Object { $_.name.ToLower() }
    }
}
catch {
    Write-Warning "Could not read verified domains (Directory.Read.All not granted?) - external-user detection will be skipped for this run. Underlying error: $($_.Exception.Message)"
}

# ---- Enumerate every site in the tenant ------------------------------------
Write-Output "Enumerating sites tenant-wide via Microsoft Graph (getAllSites)..."
$sitesUri = "https://graph.microsoft.com/v1.0/sites/getAllSites?`$select=id,name,displayName,webUrl,isPersonalSite&`$top=200"

try {
    $allSites = Get-GraphCollection -Uri $sitesUri
}
catch {
    throw "Failed to enumerate sites via /sites/getAllSites. Confirm Sites.Read.All is granted (application permission) to the managed identity's service principal. Underlying error: $($_.Exception.Message)"
}

if (-not $IncludeOneDriveSites) {
    $allSites = $allSites | Where-Object { -not $_.isPersonalSite }
}
foreach ($pattern in $ExcludedUrlPatterns) {
    $allSites = $allSites | Where-Object { $_.webUrl -notlike $pattern }
}
if ($MaxSitesToProcess -gt 0 -and $allSites.Count -gt $MaxSitesToProcess) {
    Write-Output "MaxSitesToProcess=$MaxSitesToProcess set - trimming from $($allSites.Count) sites."
    $allSites = $allSites | Select-Object -First $MaxSitesToProcess
}

Write-Output "Processing $($allSites.Count) site(s) - checking every document library's root permissions."

# ---- Walk each site's drives and their root permissions --------------------
$results   = New-Object System.Collections.Generic.List[object]
$processed = 0

foreach ($site in $allSites) {

    $processed++
    if ($processed % 25 -eq 0) { Write-Output "  ...$processed / $($allSites.Count) sites processed" }

    try {
        $drives = Get-GraphCollection -Uri "https://graph.microsoft.com/v1.0/sites/$($site.id)/drives?`$select=id,name,webUrl"

        if (-not $drives -or $drives.Count -eq 0) {
            $results.Add([PSCustomObject]@{
                SiteUrl = $site.webUrl; SiteName = $site.displayName; DriveName = ""
                PermissionType = ""; GrantedTo = ""; LinkScope = ""; LinkType = ""; Roles = ""
                IsExternal = $false; HasPassword = $false; ExpirationDateTime = ""
                Status = "NoDrives"; RecommendedAction = "OK"
            }) | Out-Null
            continue
        }

        foreach ($drive in $drives) {
            $perms = Get-GraphCollection -Uri "https://graph.microsoft.com/v1.0/sites/$($site.id)/drives/$($drive.id)/root/permissions"

            foreach ($perm in $perms) {

                $isLink    = $null -ne $perm.link
                $linkScope = if ($isLink) { $perm.link.scope } else { "" }
                $linkType  = if ($isLink) { $perm.link.type } else { "" }

                # Grantee emails come from three possible shapes: a direct
                # grant (grantedToV2), a link that's been redeemed by one or
                # more people (grantedToIdentitiesV2), or a pending sharing
                # invitation that hasn't been accepted yet (invitation.email).
                $emails = @()
                if ($perm.grantedToV2 -and $perm.grantedToV2.user -and $perm.grantedToV2.user.email) {
                    $emails += $perm.grantedToV2.user.email
                }
                if ($perm.grantedToIdentitiesV2) {
                    foreach ($identity in $perm.grantedToIdentitiesV2) {
                        if ($identity.user -and $identity.user.email) { $emails += $identity.user.email }
                    }
                }
                if ($perm.invitation -and $perm.invitation.email) { $emails += $perm.invitation.email }
                $emails = $emails | Where-Object { $_ } | Sort-Object -Unique

                $isExternal = $false
                if ($emails.Count -gt 0 -and $verifiedDomains.Count -gt 0) {
                    $internalMatchFound = $emails | ForEach-Object {
                        $parts = $_ -split '@'
                        if ($parts.Count -eq 2) { $parts[1].ToLower() }
                    } | Where-Object { $verifiedDomains -contains $_ } | Select-Object -First 1
                    $isExternal = -not [bool]$internalMatchFound
                }

                $permType =
                    if ($linkScope -eq "anonymous")        { "AnonymousLink" }
                    elseif ($linkScope -eq "organization") { "OrganizationLink" }
                    elseif ($isLink)                        { "OtherLink" }
                    else                                     { "Direct" }

                $recommendedAction =
                    if ($permType -eq "AnonymousLink" -and $FlagAnonymousLinks)          { "Review-Anonymous-Link" }
                    elseif ($permType -eq "OrganizationLink" -and $FlagOrganizationLinks) { "Review-OrgWide-Link" }
                    elseif ($isExternal)                                                  { "Review-External-Access" }
                    else                                                                  { "OK" }

                $results.Add([PSCustomObject]@{
                    SiteUrl            = $site.webUrl
                    SiteName           = $site.displayName
                    DriveName          = $drive.name
                    PermissionType     = $permType
                    GrantedTo          = ConvertTo-JoinedNames -Names $emails -MaxNames $MaxNamesPerCell
                    LinkScope          = $linkScope
                    LinkType           = $linkType
                    Roles              = ($perm.roles -join ",")
                    IsExternal         = $isExternal
                    HasPassword        = [bool]$perm.hasPassword
                    ExpirationDateTime = $perm.expirationDateTime
                    Status             = "OK"
                    RecommendedAction  = $recommendedAction
                }) | Out-Null
            }
        }
    }
    catch {
        Write-Warning "Could not read drive/permission data for $($site.webUrl): $($_.Exception.Message)"
        $results.Add([PSCustomObject]@{
            SiteUrl = $site.webUrl; SiteName = $site.displayName; DriveName = ""
            PermissionType = ""; GrantedTo = ""; LinkScope = ""; LinkType = ""; Roles = ""
            IsExternal = $false; HasPassword = $false; ExpirationDateTime = ""
            Status = "AccessDenied"; RecommendedAction = "Grant-Access-Needed"
        }) | Out-Null
    }
}

# ---- Export, ranked by risk -------------------------------------------------
$riskRank = @{
    "Review-Anonymous-Link"   = 0
    "Review-External-Access"  = 1
    "Review-OrgWide-Link"     = 2
    "Grant-Access-Needed"     = 3
    "OK"                      = 4
}
$export = $results | Sort-Object @{Expression = { $riskRank[$_.RecommendedAction] }}, SiteUrl
$export | Export-Csv -Path $outFile -NoTypeInformation -Encoding UTF8

# ---- Summary -----------------------------------------------------------------
$totalRows           = $results.Count
$sitesProcessed       = $allSites.Count
$anonymousCount       = ($results | Where-Object { $_.RecommendedAction -eq "Review-Anonymous-Link" }).Count
$orgWideCount         = ($results | Where-Object { $_.RecommendedAction -eq "Review-OrgWide-Link" }).Count
$externalCount        = ($results | Where-Object { $_.RecommendedAction -eq "Review-External-Access" }).Count
$accessDeniedCount    = ($results | Where-Object { $_.Status -eq "AccessDenied" }).Count

Write-Output "Sites processed: $sitesProcessed | Permission rows: $totalRows | Anonymous links: $anonymousCount | Org-wide links: $orgWideCount | External grants: $externalCount | AccessDenied: $accessDeniedCount"

$topRows = $export | Where-Object { $_.RecommendedAction -ne "OK" } |
    Select-Object -First 20 | ForEach-Object {
        "<tr><td>$($_.SiteUrl)</td><td>$($_.DriveName)</td><td>$($_.PermissionType)</td><td>$($_.GrantedTo)</td><td>$($_.RecommendedAction)</td></tr>"
    }

$accessDeniedWarning = if ($accessDeniedCount -gt 0) {
    "<p style='color:#b00'><b>Warning:</b> $accessDeniedCount site(s) could not be read (Access Denied) - see the attachment. Confirm Sites.Read.All is granted before assuming these have no exposure.</p>"
} else { "" }

$bodyHtml = @"
<p>SharePoint sharing exposure audit (Microsoft Graph only) - $sitesProcessed site(s) checked, $totalRows permission row(s) found on document library roots.</p>
$accessDeniedWarning
<ul>
  <li><b>$anonymousCount</b> anonymous ("anyone") link(s) found - highest exposure, review first</li>
  <li><b>$orgWideCount</b> organization-wide link(s) found</li>
  <li><b>$externalCount</b> direct grant(s) or invitation(s) to an external/guest email address</li>
  <li><b>$accessDeniedCount</b> site(s) the identity could not read</li>
</ul>
<p>Highest-priority rows:</p>
<table border='1' cellpadding='4' cellspacing='0' style='border-collapse:collapse;font-family:Segoe UI,Arial;font-size:12px'>
<tr style='background:#f2f2f2'><th align='left'>Site URL</th><th align='left'>Library</th><th align='left'>Type</th><th align='left'>Granted To</th><th align='left'>Action</th></tr>
$($topRows -join "`n")
</table>
<p style='font-size:11px;color:#666'>Scope: document-library ROOT permissions only, via Microsoft Graph - no PnP.PowerShell used. Site Collection Administrators and Owners/Members/Visitors group rosters are NOT covered here (Graph has no endpoint for that) - see the separate SharePoint Site Permissions audit for that data. Item/file-level unique permissions are not enumerated. Full detail attached.</p>
"@

Send-ReportEmail -SenderMailbox $SenderMailbox -Recipients $ReportRecipients `
    -Subject "M365 Audit: SharePoint Sharing Exposure ($timestamp)" -BodyHtml $bodyHtml -AttachmentPath $outFile

Remove-Item $outFile -Force -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue
Disconnect-MgGraph | Out-Null
Write-Output "Done."
